From: Rob Vogelaar <rob.vogelaar@libertyglobal.com>
Date: Tue, 25 Aug 2026 14:10:00 -0700
Subject: [PATCH] agent: release command data-model station objects

Every periodic AP/STA metrics event is decoded into a temporary data model and
then copied into one or more commands.  The copy operation allocates a
dm_sta_t for every station.  dm_easy_mesh_t::deinit() removed those objects
from the maps but never deleted them, so the agent retained every command's
station snapshot.  On a live five-client extender this grew agent PSS by about
62 MiB/hour.

Give every cloned map its own station objects, delete owned station and scan
objects during deinit, and clear the map pointers after destruction.  Release
the temporary decoder models once their commands own their copies.  Decode
link metrics before constructing the command so the command receives the
current report directly and no longer needs the unsafe pointer-sharing clone.

Upstream-Status: Pending
